PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"## Assessment at 2026-02-10 09:05 UTC\n\n**New information**\n- The `2026-02-10` capability bulletin changes only **V3’s published minimum operating temperature: -10 °C → 0 °C**. It remains **UNACCEPTED** candidate data; the canonical file is unchanged.\n- The `2026-02-08` Solaris correspondence is still only a promise: no certificate, number, issuing body or test standard. It does not change any published rating.\n- The `2026-02-10` newsletter is irrelevant to the technical or financial programme.\n\n**Technical position**\n- **Site A:** V1 remains compliant (-20 °C vs -12 °C); V4 also meets the temperature requirement.\n- **Site B:** V3 is the only coastal-rated vendor. Under accepted data it is rated -10 °C, but under the candidate bulletin it is rated **0 °C**, which fails the required -4 °C. If the bulletin is accepted, **no vendor in the current set is compliant for Site B**. The certificate promise does not cure this.\n- **Site C:** V3 remains compliant (750 mm; 0 °C is below the 2 °C site minimum). V2 (650 mm, -5 °C) is a compliant lower-cost alternative.\n\n**Existing plan**\nThe existing V1/V3/V3 plan and £104,900 envelope are **not justified as a complete compliant plan if the bulletin is accepted**. Under that data there is no Site B vendor, so no complete compliant cost envelope exists. No Site B order should be placed on either rating until the capability data is resolved through the authorised intake. R3 must not be relaxed to fit available vendors.\n\n## Recorded actions\n- Completed a technical-refresh work product based on both the accepted data and the unaccepted candidate; it explicitly preserves the distinction and records the Site B failure under the bulletin. The attempt is completed and gate-passed, awaiting programme-lead promotion.\n- Recorded journal entries covering:\n  - the negative finding that the bulletin removes V3 from the Site B fit;\n  - the open question of whether the bulletin should be accepted;\n  - the need for an authorised Site B route if it is accepted;\n  - proposed follow-on actions.\n- Did **not** alter canonical `sources/vendor-capabilities.csv`; the candidate remains unaccepted.\n\n## Next useful actions\n1. **Authorised intake:** apply the exact bytes of `inbox/2026-02-10/vendor-capabilities.csv` (sha256 `0e997cbc…3f920c`) to `sources/vendor-capabilities.csv` for programme-lead acceptance or rejection.\n2. After intake, re-run the per-site technical fit and update the technical work product.\n3. Refresh the cost/schedule envelope against accepted data; if Site B has no compliant vendor, record that no complete compliant envelope can be produced.\n4. Programme lead to decide the authorised Site B route: obtain a compliant coastal-rated vendor, seek a grant variation, or change the site scope.\n5. Keep the Solaris certificate open question open; do not treat the promise as evidence.","toolCalls":["tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_status","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_manage","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_preview","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","too